From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] core: a switch for per-user launchds

On macOS, PID 1 answers a non-root client's bootstrap lookup or
registration with VPROC_ERR_TRY_PER_USER, and the client asks for its
user's per-user context, a second launchd that PID 1 starts for that user;
embedded launchd serves every user from PID 1. Add HAVE_PER_USER_LAUNCHD
(config.h; default !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED, so macOS's behaviour) for the
three places that choose, so the build can pick embedded's.

NeoDarwin builds it off (docs/base/session.md, "PAM"): PID 1 and a
per-user launchd exchange jobs and ports in MIG messages with out-of-line
port arrays of moved send rights (job.defs: take_subset, lookup_children,
legacy_ipc_request). xnu-12377 refuses those from a platform binary
(IPC_POLICY_ENHANCED_V2: only COPY_SEND arrays, to ports that accept them)
with a fatal guard exception: the first non-root login killed PID 1
(EXC_GUARD, kGUARD_EXC_DESCRIPTOR_VIOLATION) and the kernel panicked. With
the boot-arg ool_port_array_enforced=0, PID 1 survives, and the per-user
launchd it starts is killed instead.

Rebase-risk: low (three #if conditions and one config.h switch).
---
--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -34,6 +34,14 @@
 #define HAVE_LIBAUDITD !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
 #endif
 
+/* Per-user launchds: PID 1 sends non-root clients' lookups, registrations
+ * and per-user context requests to a launchd it starts for their user, as on
+ * macOS; without them it serves every user itself, as on embedded.
+ */
+#ifndef HAVE_PER_USER_LAUNCHD
+#define HAVE_PER_USER_LAUNCHD !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
+#endif
+
 #ifndef HAVE_SYSTEMSTATS
 #if !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED && __has_include(<systemstats/systemstats.h>)
 #define HAVE_SYSTEMSTATS 1
--- a/src/core.c
+++ b/src/core.c
@@ -8852,7 +8852,7 @@
 		return BOOTSTRAP_UNKNOWN_SERVICE;
 	}
 
-#if TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
+#if !HAVE_PER_USER_LAUNCHD
 	// There is no need for per-user launchd's on embedded.
 	job_log(j, LOG_ERR, "Per-user launchds are not supported on this platform.");
 	return BOOTSTRAP_UNKNOWN_SERVICE;
@@ -8993,7 +8993,7 @@
 #endif
 
 	// 5641783 for the embedded hack
-#if !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
+#if HAVE_PER_USER_LAUNCHD
 	/*
 	 * From a per-user/session launchd's perspective, SecurityAgent (UID
 	 * 92) is a rogue application (not our UID, not root and not a child of
@@ -9056,7 +9056,7 @@
 	bool xpc_req = (j->mgr->properties & BOOTSTRAP_PROPERTY_XPC_DOMAIN);
 
 	// 5641783 for the embedded hack
-#if !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
+#if HAVE_PER_USER_LAUNCHD
 	if (unlikely(pid1_magic && j->anonymous && j->mgr->parentmgr == NULL && ldc->uid != 0 && ldc->euid != 0)) {
 		return VPROC_ERR_TRY_PER_USER;
 	}
